WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.060
Welcome to Grade 2 English, Unit 9: Let's Explore the City!

2
00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:09.400
This is the last unit of Year 2,
and it takes you into a busy city.

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.020
You learn the names of city places such as the library,
the market, the shopping centre and the Ferris wheel,

4
00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:20.300
and the words you need to get around: bus,
underground, ferry, map, directions and straight ahead.

5
00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:25.040
At the city aquarium you meet the octopus,
the penguin, the turtle and the shark,

6
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:29.620
and describe them with words like
amazing, clever, huge and beautiful.

7
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:34.100
You say what you like and don't like,
give true facts in the present simple,

8
00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:37.380
and talk about what you did yesterday
and what you will do tomorrow,

9
00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:42.180
just like Amal and her brother Adam in
this unit's story, “A Big Day in the City”.

10
00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:47.260
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

11
00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:54.350
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name common
places in a city, such as the library, shopping centre,

12
00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:55.460
underground and ferry.

13
00:00:56.180 --> 00:01:00.880
You will also talk about city sounds and the
things you see, such as traffic and a helicopter.

14
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:05.500
You will also say what you like and don't
like, and agree or disagree politely.

15
00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.060
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

16
00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:14.660
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: bike, while, hope, note, stone, phone.

17
00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:19.580
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

18
00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:25.680
The reading sequence includes A Poem: “At
the Zebra Crossing” and The Aquarium Schedule.

19
00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:30.780
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

20
00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:34.340
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

21
00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:38.000
The first language focus is Likes and Dislikes.

22
00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:40.620
In a busy city there is so much to do.

23
00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:44.780
We use like and don't like to say
what we enjoy and what we do not enjoy,

24
00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.840
and we can agree or disagree with a friend without being rude.

25
00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:52.560
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

26
00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:58.240
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1 — Talk About City Places.

27
00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.320
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

28
00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:07.660
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

29
00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:09.460
You are ready to begin.

30
00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:14.420
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

31
00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:20.520
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
